      <Desc>Blindspot Collective develops transformative theatre that amplifies marginalized voices illuminates untold stories bridges disparate experiences and energizes vulnerable communities. In 2024 the organization provided arts education programs to K-12 students at schools across the county and premiered 5 original productions: "iykyk," an exploration of youth activism set on a college campus; "Dancing at the End of the World," a touring production for high school youth; "Chasing Fear," a new musical inspired by Turkish folklore; "Another Day in Paradise," a documentary play with music based on interviews with San Diegos unhoused community; and "Trash Panda-Monium," an original production for Pre-K through Third Graders that supports social and emotional learning</Desc>
